{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Wrap sets of device-adding events (spec §4, §11). chains: shared and personal are the verified membership chains of membership.json (chains[0], chains[1]); personal_current_only is the personal chain up to its first rekey plus an owner device_add whose set delivers only the current epoch. verifyDeviceWraps(chains[chain][event_seq], wraps). Checks in order: the event is genesis, device_add or member_add; wraps parse; every rcpt is a device the event adds (forbidden); key_epoch in 1..event.key_epoch and (rcpt, key_epoch) unique; completeness: a recovery-authored device_add (sas \"\") carries at least one wrap (the bundle may predate later rekeys), any other event carries a wrap at event.key_epoch for every added device (older epochs optional); finally b64 sha256(cjson(wraps sorted by rcpt, then key_epoch)) == body.wraps_digest. Input order does not matter. cases MUST pass and every wrap MUST unwrap (with the recipient device kx_secret from membership.json) to vault_keys[chain][key_epoch]; invalid MUST fail with expect_error.",
